# ROI

**Exchange-office bookkeeping, built for real currency desks.**

ROI is a PHP web application for running the day-to-day books of a currency
exchange office: customer accounts, multi-currency balances, receipts, loans,
and printable reports, with a Persian (Dari/Farsi) interface throughout.

> A [Cyborg Tech Creative Agency](https://github.com/CyborgTech-co) project.

---

## What it does

- **Customer accounts** — open and manage per-customer ledgers
- **Receipts** — credit and debit entries against any account
- **Multi-currency balances** — track holdings across several currencies at once
- **Loan tracking** — record and follow outstanding loans
- **Reports** — printable statements and summaries
- **Administration** — user and account management with role-gated access
- **Backup & restore** — export and re-import the database from the admin panel

## Tech stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Backend | PHP 7.4+, custom lightweight MVC (no framework) |
| Database | MySQL / MariaDB |
| Server | Apache with `mod_rewrite` (`.htaccess` routing) |
| Frontend | Server-rendered views, vendored assets |

## Project structure

```text
ROI/
  controllers/   # Route handlers (Admin, Login, Users, ...)
  models/        # Data-access classes
  views/         # UI templates
  libs/          # Core MVC (Bootstrap, Controller, Model, View, DB, Session)
  util/          # Shared auth helpers
  assets/        # Images and static files
  public/        # Vendor libraries
  config.php     # Database, base URL, constants
  index.php      # Entry point
  .htaccess      # URL rewrite rules
```

## Getting started

Requirements: PHP 7.4+, MySQL/MariaDB, Apache with `mod_rewrite` and
`AllowOverride All` for the project path.

1. Place the project under your web root (e.g. `htdocs/ROI`).
2. Create a database and import the schema.
3. Set database credentials and the base `URL` in `config.php`.
4. Ensure `assets/user_images/` and the log path are writable.
5. Open `http://<host>/ROI/`.

## Routing

Routes resolve through `.htaccess` + `index.php` as `/controller/method/params`:

| Route | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `/ROI/` | Login |
| `/ROI/admin` | Dashboard |
| `/ROI/admin/customers` | Customer accounts |
| `/ROI/admin/receipt` | Receipts |
| `/ROI/admin/loan` | Loans |
| `/ROI/admin/reports` | Reports |
| `/ROI/admin/backres` | Backup / restore |

## Configuration

All app config lives in `config.php`: database credentials, base-URL checks,
password/session hashing keys, and currency definitions. If the deployment URL
changes, update `URL` there — the app validates the host and will redirect on a
mismatch.

## Security

- Rotate the crypto keys in `config.php` before any production deployment.
- Keep secrets out of version control; use environment-based config in production.
- Serve over HTTPS with secure session and cookie settings.

